## Open Thesis Topics
The following thesis topics are currently available

* Implementation of a consistent query answering algorithm for databases (Master/Bachelor, proficiency in Java/Python required)
* Applying SAT/ASP techniques to develop new algorithms for consistent query answering (Master, knowledge of relational databases required)
* Argumentation for conflict-resolution, social choice, and explainable AI (Master/Bachelor, apply theory to practical challenges)
* Planning in multiagent systems (Master/Bachelor, interest in agentic AI and LLMs for planning)

## Research Interests
My research is mainly in the following areas:

* Theoretical Computer Science
* Databases and Query Answering
* Knowledge Representation and Reasoning
* Explainable AI

Feel free to write me if you are interested in collaborating (or writing a thesis) on any of the following topics.

* Formal Argumentation: Theory and Applications
* Abductive Reasoning
* Contrastive Explanations
* Reasoning with Inconsistencies 
* Description Logics
* Database Repairs and Consistent Query Answering
* (Parameterized) Complexity Theory

## Reviewing
I enjoy reviewing and have had the opportunity to review for the following conferences. 

* Sub-reviewer:​ AAAI (2021--24), IJCAI (2021--24), Euro-Par’2022, CSL’2023, KR (2023,2025,2026), FoIKS’2024, LPNMR'2024
* PC: AAMAS (since 2024), IJCAI (since 2024), AAAI (since 2025), CLAR'2025
* Journals: ACM-TOCL, Applied Sciences, Annals of Pure and Applied Logic

